   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">N/A - Project approved in December 2019</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">N/A - Project approved in December 2019</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1). Analyze data from the baseline survey and select those meeting criteria to be project participants, and conduct random assignments (treatment and control groups)
2). Conduct early impact assessment 
3). Provide literacy training/financial inclusion to both treatment groups
4). Provide behavior change communication to both treatment groups
5). Analyze and develop advocacy papers and proposals</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1). Assignment of project participants into treatment and control groups completed: asset group (799 households), cash group (788 households) and control group (827 households). 799 households already received their productive assets (100 percent); 799 households in asset groups received technical assistance and training based on their income generating activities (productive assets); monthly cash for consumption support transferred to 1,587 households. 788 households in the cash group (100%) received one off lump sum cash to start/expand income generating activities.
2). Early impact assessment conducted, and report is being finalised. 
3). 1,587 households received refresher training on basic financial management/saving. 
4). 1,587 households received refresher training on family visioning (poverty graduation pathway), business plan and start up, life skills (hygiene, sanitation, household cleaning), and promoting child education.
5). Concept note for scaling up the project developed and consulted with the government for government cost sharing opportunity.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Design of local economic survey
Baseline survey is completed
Selection and assignment of project participants based on random sampling and RCT protocol
Start of poverty graduation activities, called 3 month plans for building livelihood foundation
1). Consumption support via monthly cash transfer
2). Life skills (financial inclusion and saving)
3). Selection of income generating activities (asset groups)
4). Livelihood training start from poverty graduation visioning and having a pathway</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Concept of local area economic survey was done. The roll out of the survey needs to be decided due to budget constraint
Two provincial working groups were constituted and functioned. The first meeting were organized in November 2021
2,966 IDPoor households were interviewed to assess their eligibility to be project participants
2,448 IDPoor households were selected to be project participants and assigned into asset, cash and control groups
1,587 IDPoor households already received consumption support via monthly cash transfer in October and November 2021
1,587 Wing Cards were distributed and saving accounts were opened for project participants (treatment)
90 percent of project participants (treatment groups) receiving project induction and training on family visioning, saving and financial management
Asset identification and income generating plan of the asset group is completed</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">RCT protocol, Project operation manual developed and project localities selected 
1 Project Board Meeting 
2 contract of specialized facilities (1. Graduation related works and 2. Cash transfer)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Two contracts with technical consultants - Economist and Graduation Based specialist who have a strong experience in RCT and graduation based social protection were completed.
 
RCT protocol and project operational manual was developed and being finalized by the technical consultant. The manual will provide a guidance for the project to implement the graduation based social protection that described comprehensively on how to implement it effectively. 

The first project board the formal constitution of the project board composing of co-chairs and members representing from all relevant ministries and key stakeholders. Furthermore, the project board also agreed that the project board meeting can convene with flexibility as the situation required and as needed/ deemed necessary.

The project localities analysis was done by the Technical Consultant. The project localities will be implemented at Kampong Chnang and Preah Vihear provinces where there are less development activities and fit to the graduation based project.

The grant agreement with WVI was signed off while the letter of agreement with MoSVY is on-going.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
